[Music]  today I'm going to show you how to make  a traditional mint julep one of the  oldest cocktails in existence and also  one of the best you just need three  ingredients bourbon mint and simple  syrup we're going to build this drink  right in the glass you can make it in a  glass like this this beautiful Kentucky  Derby silver cuff or ox glass works just  as well so we're going to start with a  pinch of mint eight to ten leaves half  an ounce of simple syrup  [Music]  and now muddle this just to extract the  aromatic oils in the mint but not to  pulverize it now we can add a bourbon  two and a half ounces of that when  making any cocktail measuring is really  important cocktails are all about  balance so it quote around in either  direction can sometimes make the  difference between a good and a really  bad drink so always measure if your  ingredients so we've got all our  ingredients in here and we want to add  our ice crushed ice really is best for  mint juleps because it melts a lot  faster and also stretches it out this is  a very stiff drink like 85% bourbon if  you don't have crushed ice at home you  could easily just crack some of the back  of a spoon or you can put it in a  blender or food processor but I really  recommend crushed ice just a few times  and then just give it a gentle stir just  to get that dilution going blend the  ingredients you eventually start to see  some frost appear on the outside of the  cup you'll know that the drink is ready  finish it off with a few more cubes on  top now we'll garnish it with the most  beautiful sprig of mint we can find and  you are all set and remember the mint  julep is not just for the Kentucky Derby  you can enjoy these all summer long if  you liked this video and you're looking  for more tips to step up your bartending  game subscribe to the GQ channel we've  got lots more where that came from  you  [Music]

